ght not.\n\nBut the question is whether the tiger does not see the dog. So, is it possible that the tiger does not see the dog?.\n\nYes, because the tiger could be eating the dog without seeing it. So, the statement "The tiger does not see the dog" could be true, but we don\'t have enough information to confirm it. Therefore, it\'s unknown.\n\nWait, but maybe there\'s another angle. Statement 19 says if the tiger is green and big, then it sees the dog. Since the tiger is big, but we don\'t know about green, we can\'t conclude. So, the tiger might see the dog if it\'s green, but we don\'t know. Therefore, we can\'t say for sure whether the tiger sees the dog or not. Therefore, my final option is: ']]  2%|1         | 11/600 [07:05<2:26:25, 14.92s/it]  2%|2         | 12/600 [07:12<2:02:25, 12.49s/it]
