 clear. But let\'s see if there\'s any other information that might change this.\n\nPoint 19 says if Gary is young, then Gary is round. But point 10 says Gary is red, and point 14 says all round things are young. So if Gary is round, he must be young. So Gary is both red and round, and therefore young.\n\nBut does that affect whether Gary is quiet? Point 8 says he\'s quiet, so regardless of other properties, he\'s quiet. So the statement "Gary is not quiet" would be false because Gary is quiet.\n\nI don\'t see any contradictions here. All the other points either support or don\'t affect Gary being quiet. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
