rom point 11, she\'s nice. So, according to point 16, she must be cold. But does that affect her niceness? No, because being cold doesn\'t necessarily make her not nice. In fact, she\'s nice regardless of being cold.\n\nWait, but let me make sure I\'m not missing anything. The fact that she\'s cold is a separate attribute, but niceness is already established because she\'s kind. So, her being cold doesn\'t change her niceness status.\n\nSo, putting it all together: Anne is kind → she is nice. Therefore, "Anne is not nice" is false.\n\nI don\'t see any other information that would suggest she\'s not nice. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
