g is kind and white, it\'s green. But Bob is white, but we don\'t know if he\'s kind. So, we can\'t conclude he\'s green yet.\n\n- Rule 13 says all young things are kind. So, if Bob were young, he would have to be kind.\n\n- Rule 14 says all round things are young. Since Bob is round (from rule 11), he must be young.\n\nWait, that seems to directly answer the question. Because if all round things are young, and Bob is round, then Bob must be young. Therefore, Bob is young, which means the statement "Bob is not young" would be false.\n\nBut let me double-check to make sure I\'m not missing anything. Let\'s go through each relevant rule again.\n\n- Bob is quiet and white. White things are round, so Bob is round.\n\n- All round things are young. Therefore, Bob is young.\n\nSo, yes, Bob must be young. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
