messages:   24%|##4       | 146/600 [54:14<32:21,  4.28s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nErin is big. Erin is green. Erin is kind. Erin is quiet. Erin is red. Erin is smart. Fiona is big. Gary is rough. Harry is quiet. Harry is smart. All smart people are kind. If Harry is rough and Harry is red then Harry is quiet. If someone is green then they are smart. All kind people are quiet. If someone is rough and big then they are green. Rough people are big.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Gary is big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown. I think the correct option is: B\n', '<think>.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "Gary is big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context. Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the facts provided:.\n\n1. Erin is big.\n2. Erin is green.\n3. Erin is kind.\n4. Erin is quiet.\n5. Erin is red.\n6. Erin is smart.\n7. Fiona is big.\n8. Gary is rough.\n9. Harry is quiet.\n10. Harry is smart.\n11. All smart people are kind.\n12. If Harry is rough and red, then Harry is quiet.\n13. If someone is green, then they are smart.\n14. All kind people are quiet.\n15. If someone is rough and big, then they are green.\n16. Rough people are big.\n\nNow, the question is about Gary being big. Let\'s see what we know about Gary.\n\nFrom point 8, Gary is rough. So Gary is rough. Now, looking at the rules, point 16 says that rough people are big. So if Gary is rough, then he must be big. That seems straightforward.\n\nWait, but let me check if there\'s any conflicting information. Point 15 says that if someone is rough and big, then they are green. So if Gary is rough and big, then he must be green. But do we know if Gary is green?.\n\nLooking at the facts, Erin is green, but there\'s no information about Gary\'s color. So we don\'t know if Gary is green or not. However, the question is only about whether Gary is big, not his color.\n\nSo, based on point 16, since Gary is rough, he must be big. There\'s no information that contradicts this. Even though we don\'t know if Gary is green, that doesn\'t affect his size. So the statement "Gary is big" should be true.\n\nI don\'t see any other rules that would make this false. The only thing we\'re unsure about is Gary\'s color, but that\'s irrelevant to the question about his size. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
