re rough. So, since Charlie is blue, he must be rough. Therefore, Charlie is rough.\n\nWait, but the question is asking if Charlie is not rough. If Charlie is rough, then "Charlie is not rough" would be false. So, the statement is false.\n\nBut let me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything.\n\nCharlie is green (point 5). All green things are blue (point 13). All blue things are rough (point 8). So, Charlie is rough. Therefore, the statement "Charlie is not rough" is false.\n\nI don\'t see any contradictions or missing information here. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
