messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is big. Anne is blue. Anne is rough. Bob is cold. Bob is green. Bob is rough. Bob is white. Dave is blue. Dave is white. Harry is young. If Bob is big then Bob is white. Young people are white. Cold, young people are rough. If Anne is green and Anne is young then Anne is white. White, big people are blue. All blue people are green. If someone is young and white then they are big. Blue people are cold.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Dave is not big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown. I think the correct option is: B\n', '<think>.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "Dave is not big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context. Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the facts provided:.\n\n1. Anne is big.\n2. Anne is blue.\n3. Anne is rough.\n4. Bob is cold.\n5. Bob is green.\n6. Bob is rough.\n7. Bob is white.\n8. Dave is blue.\n9. Dave is white.\n10. Harry is young.\n11. If Bob is big, then Bob is white.\n12. Young people are white.\n13. Cold, young people are rough.\n14. If Anne is green and Anne is young, then Anne is white.\n15. White, big people are blue.\n16. All blue people are green.\n17. If someone is young and white, then they are big.\n18. Blue people are cold.\n\nNow, the question is about Dave. We need to determine if Dave is not big, which would mean Dave is small.\n\nLooking at the facts, Dave is blue (fact 8) and Dave is white (fact 9). So Dave is both blue and white.\n\nFrom fact 15: White, big people are blue. That means if someone is big and white, they must be blue. But Dave is blue and white, so does that mean he\'s big? Let\'s see.\n\nFact 17 says if someone is young and white, then they are big. But Dave isn\'t necessarily young. Harry is young (fact 10), but there\'s no info on Dave\'s age.\n\nFact 18: Blue people are cold. Since Dave is blue, he must be cold. But from the facts, Bob is cold (fact 4), and Dave is white (fact 9). There\'s no direct link between being cold and being big or small.\n\nWait, fact 15 says white, big people are blue. So if someone is big and white, they\'re blue. But Dave is blue and white. So does that mean he\'s big? Because if he were big, then he would have to be blue, which he is. But the fact doesn\'t say that all blue and white people are big, only that if someone is big and white, they\'re blue. So it\'s possible that Dave is big, but it\'s also possible that he\'s not, as long as he\'s blue and white.\n\nBut wait, fact 17 says if someone is young and white, they\'re big. But Dave isn\'t necessarily young. So maybe Dave is not big because he\'s not young, even though he\'s white and blue.\n\nAlternatively, maybe being white and blue doesn\'t necessarily make someone big. The only thing we know is that if someone is big and white, they\'re blue. But Dave is blue and white, so he could be big or not. But the question is whether he is not big. So is it possible that Dave is not big?.\n\nWait, let\'s think again. If someone is big, they must be blue (from fact 15: White, big people are blue). But Dave is blue, so he could be big or not. However, fact 17 says that if someone is young and white, they\'re big. But Dave isn\'t necessarily young. So maybe Dave is not big because he\'s not young, even though he\'s white and blue.\n\nBut wait, the facts don\'t specify that only young white people are big. They just say that if someone is young and white, they\'re big. It doesn\'t say that all big people are young or that only young people are big. So maybe there are big people who are not young, but they would have to be white and blue.\n\nBut Dave is white and blue. So if he\'s big, he would fit the condition of being big and white, making him blue, which he is. But the facts don\'t explicitly say that all blue and white people are big. So it\'s possible that Dave is big, but it\'s also possible that he\'s not.\n\nWait, but the question is whether Dave is not big. So is it possible that Dave is not big? Yes, because the facts don\'t specify that he must be big. He could be small. So the statement "Dave is not big" could be true, but we don\'t have enough information to confirm it. Therefore, the answer might be unknown.\n\nWait, but let me check again. Fact 17: If someone is young and white, they are big. So if someone is young, white, and big, that\'s true. But if someone is not young, can they still be big? The fact doesn\'t say that. It only says that if someone is young and white, they\'re big. It doesn\'t say that all big people are young or that only young people can be big.\n\nSo, Dave is white and blue. If he\'s big, he would be consistent with fact 15. But since the facts don\'t specify that being white and blue implies being big, except through the condition that if someone is young and white, they\'re big, but Dave isn\'t necessarily young. Therefore, Dave could be big or not. So the statement "Dave is not big" is unknown because we don\'t have enough information to confirm it.\n\nWait, but the question is whether the statement is true, false, or unknown. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 34%|###3      | 203/600 [1:07:30<10:12,  1.54s/it]
