).\n\n### Step 3: Determine the Truth of the Statement\nThe statement in question is: \"The squirrel does not see the bear.\"\n\nFrom the given information, we know:\n- The squirrel visits the lion (Statement 11).\n- If something likes the squirrel, then the squirrel visits the rabbit (Statement 14).\n- The rabbit likes the squirrel (Statement 8).\n- The rabbit sees the bear (Statement 9).\n- The bear sees the squirrel (Statement 1).\n- The bear visits the rabbit (Statement 2).\n- The rabbit does not visit the bear (Statement 10).\n- The squirrel does not see the bear (Statement 15).\n\n### Step 4: Conclusion\nBased on the given information, we can conclude that the squirrel does not see the bear.\n\n**Answer: A) True**",
