e rules:.\n\n- All rough people are furry (point 8). So, if someone is rough, they must be furry.\n- If someone is rough and cold, then they are white (point 9). So, being rough and cold implies white.\n- All nice people are big (point 10). So, nice implies big.\n- All big people are red (point 12). So, big implies red.\n- All nice, big people are rough (point 13). So, nice and big implies rough.\n- All furry, big people are cold (point 14). So, furry and big implies cold.\n- All cold, white people are rough (point 15). So, cold and white implies rough.\n\nNow, let\'s apply this to Harry. Harry is cold (6) and white (7). So, according to point 15, if someone is cold and white, they must be rough. So, Harry is rough.\n\nFrom point 8, all rough people are furry. So, Harry is furry.\n\nFrom point 14, all furry, big people are cold. Harry is cold, so he must be big because he\'s furry and cold. So, Harry is big.\n\nFrom point 12, all big people are red. So, Harry is red.\n\nFrom point 13, all nice, big people are rough. Harry is rough and big, so he must be nice. So, Harry is nice.\n\nFrom point 10, if someone is nice, they are big. Harry is nice, so he\'s big, which we already knew.\n\nFrom point 11, furry, nice people are big. Harry is furry and nice, so he\'s big, which again we knew.\n\nSo, putting it all together, Harry is white, nice, big, rough, furry, and cold. All these attributes are consistent with the given rules. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
