messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is furry. Anne is nice. Anne is rough. Anne is white. Erin is furry. Erin is rough. Erin is white. Fiona is big. Fiona is nice. Fiona is round. Harry is nice. Harry is rough. All furry things are white. If Harry is red then Harry is round. All round, red things are furry. If Harry is rough then Harry is round. Nice, red things are big. Round, red things are white. All nice, white things are red. If something is round then it is furry.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Harry is big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown. I think the correct option is: C\n', '<think>.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "Harry is big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context. Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the facts provided:.\n\n1. Anne is furry, nice, rough, and white.\n2. Erin is furry, rough, and white.\n3. Fiona is big, nice, and round.\n4. Harry is nice and rough.\n5. All furry things are white.\n6. If Harry is red, then Harry is round.\n7. All round, red things are furry.\n8. If Harry is rough, then Harry is round.\n9. Nice, red things are big.\n10. Round, red things are white.\n11. All nice, white things are red.\n12. If something is round, then it is furry.\n\nNow, the question is about Harry being big. Let\'s break down what we know about Harry.\n\nFrom point 4, Harry is nice and rough. From point 8, if Harry is rough, then he is round. So, Harry is round.\n\nFrom point 6, if Harry were red, he would be round. But we don\'t know if Harry is red yet. However, from point 10, round, red things are white. So, if Harry is red and round, he must be white.\n\nBut wait, from point 12, if something is round, it\'s furry. So Harry, being round, is furry. From point 1, all furry things are white, so Harry must be white.\n\nNow, from point 11, all nice, white things are red. Harry is nice and white, so he must be red.\n\nSo, Harry is red, white, and round. From point 9, nice, red things are big. Since Harry is nice and red, he must be big. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
