messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nBob is rough. Fiona is cold. Fiona is rough. Gary is big. Gary is quiet. Harry is big. Harry is rough. If someone is white and smart then they are furry. All rough people are big. All furry people are white. If someone is quiet and cold then they are white. All furry people are white. If Harry is big then Harry is cold. Big, smart people are quiet. If someone is big then they are smart.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Gary is furry.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown. I think the correct option is: B\n', '<think>.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether Gary is furry based on the given context. Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the facts provided:.\n\n1. Bob is rough.\n2. Fiona is cold.\n3. Fiona is rough.\n4. Gary is big.\n5. Gary is quiet.\n6. Harry is big.\n7. Harry is rough.\n8. If someone is white and smart, then they are furry.\n9. All rough people are big.\n10. All furry people are white.\n11. If someone is quiet and cold, then they are white.\n12. All furry people are white. (This seems similar to point 10, maybe a duplicate or emphasis.).\n13. If Harry is big, then Harry is cold.\n14. Big, smart people are quiet.\n15. If someone is big, then they are smart.\n\nNow, the question is whether Gary is furry. Let\'s break it down.\n\nFrom point 4, Gary is big. From point 15, if someone is big, then they are smart. So Gary is smart.\n\nFrom point 14, big, smart people are quiet. Since Gary is both big and smart, he must be quiet. But wait, point 5 already says Gary is quiet, so that\'s consistent.\n\nNow, looking at point 13: If Harry is big, then Harry is cold. Harry is big (point 6), so according to this, Harry should be cold. But I don\'t see any information stating that Harry is cold. So we don\'t know if Harry is cold or not.\n\nMoving on, point 11 says if someone is quiet and cold, then they are white. But we don\'t know if Harry is cold, so we can\'t determine if Harry is white based on this.\n\nPoint 10 and 12 both state that all furry people are white. So if Gary were furry, he would have to be white.\n\nBut do we have any information that connects Gary\'s furiteness to his other attributes? Let\'s see.\n\nFrom point 4, Gary is big. From point 15, big people are smart. From point 14, big, smart people are quiet. So Gary is quiet.\n\nBut how does that help us determine if he\'s furry? We need to see if there\'s a rule that links being quiet or something else to being furry.\n\nLooking at point 11 again: If someone is quiet and cold, then they are white. But we don\'t know if Gary is cold. We only know he\'s quiet.\n\nWait, point 13 says if Harry is big, he\'s cold. But we don\'t know if Harry is cold. So maybe Harry isn\'t cold, but that doesn\'t affect Gary.\n\nSo, do we have any rule that says if someone is quiet, they are furry? No, the only rule about being furry is that all furry people are white, and if someone is white and smart, they are furry.\n\nBut we don\'t know if Gary is white or not. We know he\'s quiet, but nothing connects quietness to being white or furry.\n\nWait, let\'s think again. All furry people are white. So if Gary were furry, he\'d be white. But is there any way to determine if he\'s white?.\n\nLooking at point 11: If someone is quiet and cold, they are white. But Gary is quiet, but we don\'t know if he\'s cold. So we can\'t conclude he\'s white based on that.\n\nIs there any other way Gary could be white? Maybe through other people. For example, Fiona is cold and rough (points 2 and 3). If someone is quiet and cold, they\'re white. But Fiona is cold but not quiet (point 5 says Fiona is rough, which we know from point 3). Wait, point 5 says Fiona is rough, and point 3 says she\'s rough. So Fiona is cold and rough, but not quiet. So she doesn\'t fall under the "quiet and cold" category.\n\nHarry is big and rough (points 6 and 7). If Harry is big, he\'s cold (point 13). But we don\'t know if he\'s quiet. So Harry\'s status is big, cold, rough, but we don\'t know if he\'s smart or white.\n\nWait, point 14 says big, smart people are quiet. So if Harry is big (he is), and if he\'s smart, he\'s quiet. But do we know if Harry is smart? From point 15, big people are smart, so Harry is smart. Therefore, Harry is quiet. But wait, point 13 says if Harry is big, he\'s cold, but doesn\'t say anything about him being quiet. However, point 14 says big, smart people are quiet. Since Harry is big and smart, he must be quiet. So Harry is quiet.\n\nBut does that help us with Gary? No, because Gary is separate. So Gary is quiet, but we don\'t know if he\'s cold or smart. Wait, Gary is big (point 4), so he\'s smart (point 15). So Gary is smart and big, which makes him quiet (point 14). So Gary is quiet.\n\nBut how does that help us with being furry? We know all furry people are white, but we don\'t know if Gary is white. The only way Gary could be white is if he\'s furry, but we don\'t have any information that connects his quietness to being white or furry.\n\nWait, let\'s look at point 11 again: If someone is quiet and cold, then they are white. But Gary is quiet, but we don\'t know if he\'s cold. So we can\'t conclude he\'s white.\n\nIs there any other rule that could link Gary\'s attributes to being white or furry? I don\'t think so. The only connection is that if someone is white and smart, they\'re furry. But we don\'t know if Gary is white or smart beyond what we\'ve deduced.\n\nWait, Gary is smart because he\'s big (point 15). So he\'s smart and big. From point 14, big, smart people are quiet, which we already know. But does being smart and big make him white? No, because the rule is that if someone is white and smart, they\'re furry. It doesn\'t say that all smart and big people are white.\n\nSo, to summarize: Gary is big, so he\'s smart. Big, smart people are quiet. So Gary is quiet. But we don\'t know if he\'s white or not. Since all furry people are white, but we don\'t know if Gary is white, we can\'t conclude if he\'s furry. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 60%|#####9    | 359/600 [1:34:26<23:07,  5.76s/it]
