messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is nice. Anne is white. Anne is young. Dave is cold. Dave is nice. Dave is smart. Erin is cold. Erin is not kind. Erin is not nice. Erin is smart. Erin is young. Fiona is kind. Smart people are white. Kind, cold people are smart. Kind people are big. If Fiona is cold and Fiona is big then Fiona is nice. If someone is nice and big then they are cold. If someone is young and white then they are cold. If Anne is nice then Anne is cold. Big, young people are nice. Big people are young.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Fiona is not big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown. I think the correct option is: C\n', '<think>.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "Fiona is not big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context. Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the facts provided:.\n\n1. Anne is nice.\n2. Anne is white.\n3. Anne is young.\n4. Dave is cold.\n5. Dave is nice.\n6. Dave is smart.\n7. Erin is cold.\n8. Erin is not kind.\n9. Erin is not nice.\n10. Erin is smart.\n11. Erin is young.\n12. Fiona is kind.\n13. Smart people are white.\n14. Kind, cold people are smart.\n15. Kind people are big.\n16. If Fiona is cold and Fiona is big, then Fiona is nice.\n17. If someone is nice and big, then they are cold.\n18. If someone is young and white, then they are cold.\n19. If Anne is nice, then Anne is cold.\n20. Big, young people are nice.\n21. Big people are young.\n\nNow, the question is about Fiona. Specifically, is she not big? So I need to determine if Fiona is big or not based on these statements.\n\nLet\'s start by looking at what we know about Fiona. From point 12, Fiona is kind. From point 15, kind people are big. So if Fiona is kind, then she must be big. That seems straightforward.\n\nWait, but let me check if there\'s any information that contradicts this. Point 16 says that if Fiona is cold and big, then she\'s nice. But we don\'t know if Fiona is cold. However, point 14 says that kind, cold people are smart. Since Fiona is kind, if she were cold, she would be smart. But we don\'t have any information about her being cold or not.\n\nPoint 19 says if Anne is nice, then she\'s cold. We know Anne is nice (point 1), so from that, Anne is cold (point 19). But that doesn\'t affect Fiona directly.\n\nPoint 20 says big, young people are nice. So if Fiona is big and young, she\'s nice. But we don\'t know if she\'s young. Point 21 says big people are young, so if she\'s big, she must be young. So if she\'s big, she\'s young, and thus, according to point 20, she\'s nice.\n\nBut wait, from point 15, kind people are big, and Fiona is kind, so she must be big. Therefore, she\'s big, which makes her young (from point 21), and thus, she\'s nice (from point 20). So Fiona is nice, which would mean she\'s cold if she\'s big and nice? Wait, no, point 17 says if someone is nice and big, they\'re cold. So if Fiona is nice and big, she\'s cold. But from point 15, she\'s kind, so she\'s big, and from point 14, if she\'s kind and cold, she\'s smart. But we don\'t know if she\'s cold yet.\n\nWait, but from point 15, kind people are big, so Fiona is big. From point 21, big people are young, so she\'s young. From point 20, big, young people are nice, so she\'s nice. From point 17, if she\'s nice and big, she\'s cold. So she\'s cold. But from point 14, if she\'s kind and cold, she\'s smart. But we don\'t know if she\'s cold yet, but from the previous deduction, she is cold because she\'s nice and big.\n\nSo, putting it all together: Fiona is kind (12), so she\'s big (15). Being big makes her young (21), which makes her nice (20). Being nice and big makes her cold (17). So she\'s cold, but that\'s okay because the question is about her being big. Since she\'s big, the statement "Fiona is not big" would be false.\n\nWait, but let me double-check. Is there any possibility that Fiona isn\'t big? From point 15, kind people are big, and Fiona is kind, so she must be big. There\'s no way around that. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 61%|######1   | 366/600 [1:36:23<1:35:52, 24.58s/it]
