e and big, it\'s young. So if Bob is nice and big, he must be young. But we don\'t know if Bob is big. If Bob were big, he\'d have to be young. But Bob is kind and nice, but we don\'t know about his size.\n\nPoint 17 says young, big things are kind. So if Bob is young and big, he\'s kind. But Bob is kind, but we don\'t know if he\'s big or young.\n\nSo, can we conclude anything about Bob\'s size? We know Bob is kind and nice, but nothing about his size. The only information about size is that Charlie is big and green, and Anne is big because she\'s green. But Bob\'s size isn\'t mentioned.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, we can\'t determine if Bob is big or not. So the statement "Bob is not big" could be true or false, but we don\'t have enough information to confirm it. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 62%|######1   | 371/600 [1:36:27<19:26,  5.10s/it]
