nd. So, maybe some cold people are kind, but not all. So, if Fiona is cold, she might be kind, making her green, but we don't know. But regardless, since she's furry, she's smart.\n\nSo, circling back, Erin is cold and furry. From statement 11, being furry implies smart. So, Erin is smart. Therefore, the statement \"Erin is smart\" is true.\n\nWait, but let me make sure I'm not missing anything. Let me go through each step again.\n\n1. Erin is cold (statement 3).\n2. Erin is furry (statement 4).\n3. From statement 11: If someone is furry, they are smart. So, Erin is smart.\n\nYes, that seems solid. There's no conflicting information here. So, the answer should be A) True.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Erin is smart\" is true based on the given information.\n\n**Answer: A) True**",
