 big.\n  - We don't know if Harry is round yet.\n\n- **Statement 18:** Big people are rough.\n  - So, if Harry is big, he must be rough.\n\n- **Statement 17:** Rough, big people are furry.\n  - If Harry is both rough and big, he is furry.\n\n- **Statement 19:** If someone is furry, then they are nice.\n  - So, if Harry is furry, he is nice.\n\n### Conclusion:\n\n- We don't have direct information about Harry's niceness. All the given statements either don't specify Harry's attributes or require assumptions that aren't provided. Therefore, we can't definitively say whether Harry is nice or not based on the given information.\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\boxed{C}",
