 are young. Therefore, Erin is smart, so she must be young.\n\nFrom point 10, all young people are furry. So, since Erin is young, she is furry.\n\nWait, but the question is asking if Erin is not furry. But according to this, Erin is young, hence furry. So, the statement "Erin is not furry" would be false.\n\nBut let me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything.\n\n- Erin is red (5).\n- All red people are not round (8), so Erin is not round.\n- If Erin is red and not round, then she is nice (11). So, Erin is nice.\n- Nice people are smart (14), so Erin is smart.\n- All smart people are young (13), so Erin is young.\n- All young people are furry (10), so Erin is furry.\n\nTherefore, Erin is definitely furry, which means the statement "Erin is not furry" is false.\n\nI don\'t see any contradictions or missing information here. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
