s round, they're big. But does that mean all big people are round? No, because point 13 is a one-way implication. It doesn't say that being big implies being round.\n\nSo, Fiona is green. To be round, she needs to be big as well (from point 19). But do we have any information about Fiona's size? The facts don't mention whether Fiona is big or not. The only mention of size is about Gary: Gary is round, big, and furry (points 6, 7, 10, 13, 14). But there's no info on Fiona's size.\n\nTherefore, we can't conclude whether Fiona is round or not based on the given information. The only way to know is if she's big, but we don't have that data. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
