is nice and Fiona is young. Fact 6 says Fiona is nice. Fact 14 says nice, green things are smart. But Fiona isn\'t necessarily green, so we don\'t know if she\'s smart or not. However, that doesn\'t affect Erin.\n\nFact 10 says smart things are young. So if something is smart, it\'s young. But Erin is not young, so she can\'t be smart. Fact 14 also says nice, green things are smart, but again, that\'s about things that are both nice and green being smart, which doesn\'t apply to Erin.\n\nFact 11 says young things are kind. So if something is young, it\'s kind. But Erin is not young, so we don\'t know if she\'s kind or not. However, the statement is about Erin not being young, which is directly given as fact 5.\n\nI don\'t see any contradictions or additional information that would change this conclusion. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
